<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bafut</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1907 CE (approx.) · capital Bafut</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the largest kingdoms of the Cameroon Grassfields, whose Fon resisted German conquest and whose palace at Bafut is among the best preserved in the region.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bafut was founded by groups said to have migrated from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tikar-people">Tikar</a> area in the north-east, probably in the 18th century, and settled north of what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamenda">Bamenda</a>. Its rulers, the Fons, gradually conquered and absorbed neighbouring villages, building one of the larger chiefdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon-grassfields">Grassfields</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fon-title">Fon</a> was a sacred king, supported by palace societies, notables and a regulatory society, the Kwifon, that enforced his decisions and ritual law. The royal compound with its shrine house, the Achum, was the political and religious centre. Bafut farmed, raised livestock and took part in trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a>, kola and slaves across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon-grassfields">Grassfields</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fon-title">Fon</a> Abumbi I fought German troops in 1901 and 1907 before submitting, and Bafut was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamerun">Kamerun</a>. After 1916 it fell under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-cameroons">British Cameroons</a>. The Fon still reigns; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achirimbi-ii">Achirimbi II</a> became widely known through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-durrell">Gerald Durrell's</a> book <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-bafut-beagles">The Bafut Beagles</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1700 CE – 1907 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"